& [Observation] is asymmetric MCP evidence projection
  + selected route_attention output preserves the runtime result and independently verified admission evidence
  + runtime refusals currently collapse to adapter fault code runtime_refused and a short underlying reason
  + the verified Needle runtime commonly archives a negative run with run_id status fault and admission not_applicable

& [Intent] is equal inspectability for yes and no
  + preserve the bounded sanitized runtime fault object in structured MCP output
  + when a runtime refusal supplies a canonical run identity invoke the independent verifier before returning
  + require verified evidence kind run exact evidence identity recorded status fault and admission not_applicable
  + expose the verification next to the runtime refusal while retaining MCP isError true
  + never turn verified refusal into selection authorization or truth

& [FailureBoundary] remains fail closed
  + refusal evidence with malformed identity failed verification wrong status or admitted account returns evidence_verification_failed
  + infrastructure faults without a run identity remain adapter faults and make no fabricated evidence claim

& [Deferred] is replay of learned inference calibration changes and automatic retry
